  "facts": [
    "The Menora Tunnel, an 800‑metre marvel beneath the Keledang Range, opened on 24 September 1987 as part of Malaysia's North–South Expressway Northern Route, linking traffic through Perak's rugged terrain.",
    "Designed with twin bores, the Menora Tunnel features two side‑by‑side tubes—one for each direction—ensuring smooth flow while cutting through the Keledang Range.",
    "Despite its engineering prowess, the Menora Tunnel has earned a reputation as a frequent accident hotspot, prompting ongoing safety reviews and driver caution."
